1: //! A bounded kernel heap with a static bootstrap arena and optional frame-backed growth.
2: //!
3: //! The bootstrap arena is 256 KiB and tracks at most 128 allocations. An optional
4: //! extension maps pages on demand inside a caller-reserved virtual range, with
5: //! its own fixed allocation table and a caller-supplied transactional mapper.
6: //! Growth is bounded; allocation fails when either arena or metadata is full.
7: //!
8: //! The global wrapper serializes access with an IRQ-save spin lock. The lock
9: //! prevents a local interrupt from re-entering a held allocator lock; allocation
10: //! remains forbidden in IRQ/exception context to keep handlers bounded and
11: //! allocation-free.
